From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: 8703b: shift the LNA index for the CCK RX power

query_phy_status_cck() masks the LNA index out of bits 7:5 of the PHY
status (LNA_L_BITS) and its high bit out of bit 7 (LNA_H_BIT) without
shifting them down, then FIELD_PREP() puts them into GENMASK(2, 0) and
BIT(3), which keeps only the low bits: the LNA index is always 0.
get_cck_rx_pwr() then takes lna_gain_table[0] (-2 dB) for every frame,
whatever gain stage the AGC picked: the power of CCK frames is
-2 - 2 * VGA, off by up to 46 dB.

On an idle link nearly every frame received is a CCK beacon, so the
station's RSSI average follows these values. Read too strong, it pins
DIG's lower bound at DIG_PERF_MID (0x40): the IGI stays 10-25 dB above
the real signal, beacons are missed, and mac80211 drops the connection
after a beacon loss (the RTL8723CS on the PinePhone reconnected every
few seconds, signal jumping between -2 and -60 dBm with the phone still).

Use FIELD_GET() to extract the fields.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rtw8703b.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rtw8703b.c
@@ -903,13 +903,13 @@
 				 struct rtw_rx_pkt_stat *pkt_stat)
 {
 	struct phy_status_8703b *phy_status = (struct phy_status_8703b *)phy_raw;
-	u8 vga_idx = phy_status->cck_agc_rpt_ofdm_cfosho_a & VGA_BITS;
-	u8 lna_idx = phy_status->cck_agc_rpt_ofdm_cfosho_a & LNA_L_BITS;
+	u8 vga_idx = FIELD_GET(VGA_BITS, phy_status->cck_agc_rpt_ofdm_cfosho_a);
+	u8 lna_idx = FIELD_GET(LNA_L_BITS, phy_status->cck_agc_rpt_ofdm_cfosho_a);
 	s8 rx_power;

 	if (rtwdev->dm_info.rx_cck_agc_report_type == 1)
 		lna_idx = FIELD_PREP(BIT_LNA_H_MASK,
-				     phy_status->cck_rpt_b_ofdm_cfosho_b & LNA_H_BIT)
+				     FIELD_GET(LNA_H_BIT, phy_status->cck_rpt_b_ofdm_cfosho_b))
 			| FIELD_PREP(BIT_LNA_L_MASK, lna_idx);
 	else
 		lna_idx = FIELD_PREP(BIT_LNA_L_MASK, lna_idx);
